 Learn about Revolut Pay, a digital wallet payment method used in the United Kingdom and the European Union.
 
-Revolut Pay, developed by [Revolut](https://www.revolut.com/business/revolut-pay/), a global finance app, is a digital wallet payment method. Revolut Pay uses the customer’s stored balance or cards to fund the payment, and offers the option for non-Revolut customers to save their details after their first purchase.
+Revolut Pay is a real-time payment method for customers who have a [Revolut](https://www.revolut.com/business/revolut-pay/) account. Revolut is a licensed bank with tens of millions of customers across Europe and the UK. With Revolut Pay, customers can pay directly from their Revolut balance or linked cards without re-entering payment details.
 
-When customers select Revolut Pay as their payment method, Stripe redirects them to Revolut Pay’s website, where they have to authenticate with their account details or checkout as a first time user. After authenticating, Revolut Pay redirects customers back to your website.
+When a customer selects Revolut Pay, the checkout flow adapts to their device. On mobile, Stripe opens the Revolut app for the customer to authenticate and confirm the payment. On desktop, Stripe shows the customer a QR code to scan with the Revolut app. After confirming the payment, the customer returns to your site. Revolut Pay is available to businesses in the EU and UK and supports one-time and recurring payments.
 
